From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:18:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: apple-h9p: make the handoff link flush a separate
 opt-in

Waiting for the link-up status to fall under PERST before LTSSM is
stopped was tied to the sleep path. A warm handoff can see the same
stale status, but not every board needs the wait.

Do the flush in the outgoing kexec shutdown path only, and only when
apple,ans-kexec-link-flush is set, so it stays off unless a board asks
for it. The incoming kernel restarts the storage port with the cold-boot
power cycle, which needs no flush.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c
index 7a0a832e3..46c24f2b5 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c
@@ -3894,7 +3894,12 @@ static void apple_h9p_s8003_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			apple_cold_reset("Apple PCIe: PERST failed during handoff");
 			return;
 		}
+		if (!port && of_property_read_bool(pcie->dev->of_node, "apple,ans-kexec-link-flush")) {
+			u32 val;
 
+			readl_poll_timeout(pcie->base_port[0] + S8003_PORT_LINKSTS,
+				val, !(val & S8003_PORT_LINKSTS_UP), 100, 100000);
+		}
 		if (apple_s8003_port_stop(pcie, port)) {
 			apple_cold_reset("Apple PCIe: LTSSM stop failed during handoff");
 			return;
